From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:53:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(pm): isolate build consumer account cache [daveey]

Pin the passwd-backed account home alongside Path.home in the build adapter fixture. PR CI exposed three real-home guard failures after account cache sharing stopped following HOME. The unchanged guard and all original build assertions remain active. Proof: canonical build consumers RED 3 failures before the fixture pin; build consumers plus account-seed suite GREEN after.
---
 tests/scripts/test_pm_build_consumers.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/scripts/test_pm_build_consumers.py b/tests/scripts/test_pm_build_consumers.py
index ae05c2181c..d9c396f39a 100644
--- a/tests/scripts/test_pm_build_consumers.py
+++ b/tests/scripts/test_pm_build_consumers.py
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ import pytest
 @pytest.fixture
 def local_toolchain(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
     monkeypatch.setattr(Path, "home", lambda: tmp_path / "home")
+    monkeypatch.setattr("hermes_constants._account_home", lambda: tmp_path / "home")
     uv = shutil.which("uv")
     assert uv, "build integration tests require the dev-shell toolchain"
     monkeypatch.setattr("pm.client.is_runtime", lambda: True)
